				<p class="fine" style="margin-top:20px;max-width:660px">
					<code>{best.command}</code> carries the result and <code>{worst.command}</code> is close to a no-op. The weak row stays in the table, because quietly dropping the rows that look bad is how {stats.overallSaved} turns into a fake 90%. Most tools in this category publish one big percentage; we publish the weak rows beside the strong ones so you can find your own workload in the table. Run <code>omni stats</code> for your own.
